<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The resurrect mech ability's cast job (OverlordWarcasket.JobDriver_CastResurrectMech, whose
    header has why the ability cannot use VEF's own VFEA_GotoTargetAndUseAbility): the pilot
    walks to within cast range of the mech corpse, target A, stands through the warmup and
    casts. Named as the ability def's jobDef (AbilityDefs/ResurrectMech.xml) and ordered by the
    ability itself, as any ordered job, so holding the queue key queues it. The fields are
    VEF's job's (VEF 1.6 Defs/Abilities/GeneralAbilityDefs.xml). reportString is never shown,
    the driver reports the ability's jobReportString, as VEF's does, but it is a translatable
    field the game's walker lists, so it carries vanilla's shape of the same report.
  -->
  <JobDef>
    <defName>OLWC_CastResurrectMech</defName>
    <driverClass>OverlordWarcasket.JobDriver_CastResurrectMech</driverClass>
    <reportString>resurrecting TargetA.</reportString>
    <allowOpportunisticPrefix>true</allowOpportunisticPrefix>
    <carryThingAfterJob>true</carryThingAfterJob>
  </JobDef>
</Defs>
